    "title": "L1 marked common-pencil next-strip boundary fiber bound",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the thin boundary d+p>=(m+1)ell of strip m, put g=(m+1)ell-d. For fixed p<=P_0 and ell>2P_0, the exact list threshold forces at least m+1 dense petals. Their selected support product has degree t ell-v, so CRT leaves at most one numerator when v<g and at most q^(v-g+1)<=q^p otherwise. Thus the fixed-locator numerator fiber is polynomial uniformly on the boundary omitted by the strict Forney window.",
